---
/*
  The page Ralfs sends in the middle of a conversation. It has to stand on its
  own. Structure and copy: 04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/how-it-works",
  built on the three pillars in section 2.2.

  Sprache: einfaches Englisch, Ansage Manuel 07.09.2026 abends. Alle Befunde
  bleiben drin, nur in kurzen Saetzen. Der Satz zur Einkommenszusage unten steht
  wortgleich in scripts/allowed-phrases.txt. Wer ihn umformuliert, muss die
  Freigabezeile dort mitziehen, sonst bricht der Copy-Check.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How it works | Wunder"
  description="Three things you can check: your own portal, official tools instead of passwords, and a check on everyone who writes in your name."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>How the work is done.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Three parts. You can check each one. You do not have to take our word for it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="portal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Part one</p>
      <h2>You see the same screen we do.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You can look at your account at any time. You do not have to ask us. You see the same
        number we see.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every post goes through our own portal. We read each number at the source. We do not guess
        it. We built the whole chain ourselves. So there is nothing we could tell you that we
        cannot also show you.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          First we read your last thirty days. We look at what your account did on its own.
          That number is your starting point.
        </li>
        <li>
          Each night our system works out your middle day of the last thirty days. Then it scores
          every post against your own middle day, not against some agency average.
        </li>
        <li>
          A post is scored three days after it goes up. Before that it is too young to judge.
        </li>
        <li>
          You log into your own portal. You see views, reach and followers there. You can look
          at seven, thirty and ninety days. You see the daily line and the period before it. You
          see the content plan. You see the plan your manager wrote.
        </li>
        <li>
          Two things are missing there on purpose. You cannot see who a single fan is. You cannot
          see how our team is doing inside. That line keeps your access from becoming a back door
          into other people's data.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="portal-hint">
        <Placeholder label="Reduced hint of the portal view, no readable numbers" ratio="wide" />
        <p class="caption">
          A small hint, on purpose. The portal is not a public demo. It stays out of search.
        </p>
      </div>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="access">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Part two</p>
      <h2>You never hand us a password.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You do not give us a password. Not for Instagram. Not for OnlyFans.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work through the official tools of the platforms. We do not use your login. You give
        those tools access, and you can take it back. A password you hand over is gone.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>We post to Instagram through Zernio. It is an official tool and it plans posts for us.</li>
        <li>We run the OnlyFans chat and vault through Infloww. It is an official tool too.</li>
        <li>Our team signs in to our own systems with company Google accounts. No shared logins.</li>
        <li>
          Your portal login is its own thing. It is kept apart from the staff system. A creator
          login can never hold a staff role. We read who you are from a signed cookie only. So
          nobody can change a number in the link and land in someone else's data.
        </li>
        <li>
          We can switch your portal access off at once. It stops on the next click, not on the
          next login. Taking you out of the portal deletes nothing. It only sets a date. So a
          wrong click is one reset, not a loss.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="chatting">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Part three</p>
      <h2>We check the people who write in your name.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You already make the work. What is missing is the selling. That is the part we do, with
        people we check.
      </p>
      <p>
        Someone writes to your fans in your name. That work gets read back, and not by the person
        who wrote it. Chat is the only thing we do in your name. So we built a check for it. It
        runs to a plan, and nobody on the chat team can turn it off.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Twice a week our system reads the shift plan. It pulls the chat log of the last finished
          shift. It scores that log against a written score sheet. Every version of the sheet is
          kept.
        </li>
        <li>
          Only human messages get a score. Each message is sorted by source first. Messages sent by
          the system count as background, not as work.
        </li>
        <li>
          There is a fixed pass mark. Several people score, and we take the middle score. Some
          mistakes fail on their own. We also measure how fast the reply came.
        </li>
        <li>The chat logs themselves are never saved in the database for this report.</li>
        <li>
          Messages sent by the system pass one more test. It is built into the code. It blocks any
          message that hints at an age under eighteen. It blocks any request for money outside the
          platform. The point is simple. An automatic message must not put your account at risk.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we do not do.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No fee up front. No fee before you have earned.</li>
        <li>No access to your money. Your payout reaches your bank first.</li>
        <li>No post goes out without your yes.</li>
        <li>No old post stays in the plan once you ask us to stop it.</li>
        <li>We do not guarantee your income. Nobody honest can.</li>
      </ul>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .portal-hint {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 32px 0;
  }
</style>
